On Mon, Sep 29, 2008 at 12:34 PM, tijlan <picos.picos@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Would it be not possible to use something like "-" as a consonant
> placeholder? Example:
>
> Angela --> la .andjela-.
> Antonio --> la .antonio-.

Those two happen to be grammatical, but they are fu'ivla rather than
cmevla. (Cluster "ndj" is not allowed actually, but if it were, it
would be a fu'ivla.) But that's not always an option. For example {la
.sara-.} parses as thee cmavo: la sa ra

mu'o mi'e xorxes


